oaf of Bread","Snake Egg","Spices","Vinegar","Tundrabear Sandwich","Saucy Bearmeat","Snow Bunny Stew","Water Flask","High Quality Firing Sheet","Unfired Pot","Large Block of Clay","Pot Sketch","Metal Bits","Small Piece of Ore","Ulthork Meat Pie","Pie Tin Mold","Ceramic Lining","Quality Firing Sheet","Unfired Ceramic Lining","Small Block of Clay","Ceramic Lining Sketch","Snow Griffin Souffle","Borannin's Seal","Mordin Frostcleaver","Leif's Napkin","Oven","Guard Leif","Used Napkin","Trita's Napkin","Trita Coldheart","Dirty Pot","Brita's Napkin","Lorekeeper Brita","Used Pie Tin","Thoridain's Napkin","Grand Historian Thoridain","Seal of Thoridain","Glass Shard","Tanik's Note","Unfired Velium Vial","Velium Purifier","Velium Vial","Vial of Velium Vapors","Kromrif Death Squad","Tanik Greskil","Frundle Frenkler","A Ry`Gorr Miner","Tower of Frozen Shadow","Pottery Wheel","Kiln","Non-Tradeskill","Tanik's note","Crystalline Silk Fiber","Glowing Bile Soaker","Glowing Crystalline Silk Piece","Rexx Frostweaver","Loom","Sewing Kit","Embroidered Shawl Pattern","Spool of Sacred Coldain Thread","A Manticore","Lock of Siren Hair","A drakkel dire wolf","Runed Prayer Shawl Pattern","Blank Rune","Burin","Cutlassfish Oil","Encased Velium Etched Rune","Enchanted Velium Powder","Etched Rune","Etched Rune Pattern","Fish Oil Extractor","Fletching Kit","Liquid Velium","Mortar and Pestle","Prayer to Brell","Royal Kromrif blood","Rubbing Alcohol","Rune Casing Pattern","Rune Casing","Sacred Velium Ink","Unfired Rune","Velium Etched Rune","Platinum Bar","Runed Sea Shell","Gilthan Brittleblade","Enduring Breath","Grimthor Brewbeard","Fishing","A mortician","Brew Barrel","Jeweler's Kit","Jewelcrafting","Hand Made Backpack","Heady Kiola","Skull Ale","Excellent Siren Scales","Wenglawks Manly Purse"],"dialogue":[{"npc":"Loremaster Borannin","text":"Greetings, Soandso, please be seated and hear the Grand Historian, he is among the wisest of our people."},{"npc":"Loremaster Borannin","text":"Greetings, Soandso, please be seated and hear the Grand Historian, he is among the wisest of our people."},{"npc":"Loremaster Borannin","text":"Those eager to prove their loyalty to the Dain may do so by completing tasks that I have been commissioned to assign. If you wish to begin your service, return to me with four toes of our enemy, the Kromrif."},{"npc":"Loremaster Borannin","text":"Those eager to prove their loyalty to the Dain may do so by completing tasks that I have been commissioned to assign. If you wish to begin your service, return to me with four toes of our enemy, the Kromrif."},{"npc":"Loremaster Borannin","text":"Ahh, well done! On behalf of the Dain I thank you for making a dent in the number of our sworn enemy. Please accept this as a token of our appreciation. It is trivial, I know, but if you are as loyal as you claim to be, it will increase in power over time. It just so happens I have a [task] to further demonstrate your loyalty, Soandso."},{"npc":"Loremaster Borannin","text":"Ahh, well done! On behalf of the Dain I thank you for making a dent in the number of our sworn enemy. Please accept this as a token of our appreciation. It is trivial, I know, but if you are as loyal as you claim to be, it will increase in power over time. It just so happens I have a [task] to further demonstrate your loyalty, Soandso."},{"npc":"Loremaster Borannin","text":"Ahh yes, good to see you again Maeve . I wish it were under better circumstances that we meet today. For some time now we have sent teams of our finest rogues to gather intelligence for the Dain. Tanik Greskil is one of our best. He was recently sent into the heart of Kael Drakkel on a very important mission and has not returned. He is now long overdue, and fearing the worst, our wise council has asked me to dispatch a rescue party to determine what has become of him and return him to safety. I have decided to give you this opportunity to build upon the trust you have earned from the council. Will you accept this mission?"},{"npc":"Loremaster Borannin","text":"The council will be pleased to hear of your acceptance. Scour the regions surrounding the city of the Giants. Discover what happened to Tanik and, if possible, return him to Thurgadin. If you are successful, remember to hand me your woven shawl. We seem to be running low on them, but I must say Mordin has never had so much help in the kitchen. Anyway, I will eagerly await word of your findings. Good luck, and may Brell protect you."},{"npc":"Tanik Greskil","text":"Outlander! Thank Brell you've found me! I am the last surviving member of my unit. Our mission was somehow compromised, the bloody Kromrif knew just where to find us... I can't imagine how they knew. I was barely able to escape with my life and wandered into a trap here. I am badly hurt and need your help."},{"npc":"Tanik Greskil","text":"Quickly, give me a vial of Veluim Vapors so I can return home, I am in desperate need of some attention from our clerics."},{"npc":"Tanik Greskil","text":"Drat! Are you telling me you don't have one with you? Run back to Thurgadin at once and speak with Frundle, she can make you one. I will do what I can to stay alive. I may need to move about a bit to keep from being discovered. Hurry now outlander, you're my only hope."},{"npc":"Frundle Frenklar","text":"Ahh, you come seeking my family recipe? After all you've done for our people it's the least I can do. First you must fashion a velium vial, then combine the vial with two small pieces of velium in this jar. That's all there is to it. Please keep the recipe a secret."},{"npc":"Frundle Frenklar","text":"I'm no potter mind you, but if I remember correctly it's a small brick of velium, three crystalline silks, and two glass shards. Then you'll have to finish up by firing it in a kiln with a high quality firing sheet."},{"npc":"Tanik Greskil","text":"Thank you. I shall be eternally grateful to you. Should you ever require my assistance I pledge to you my aid. Please deliver this to Borannin, it is imperative that he deliver this to the Dain at once. Farewell for now outlander..."},{"npc":"Loremaster Borannin","text":"Words cannot express our gratitude for your deeds outlander, you have saved a hero of our people from certain death. Please accept this, the Fur-lined shawl, as a token of our sincere appreciation. You are indeed among the most highly regarded Humans to set foot in Thurgadin. The next time we meet be sure to ask me how to further advance your reputation with the Coldain."},{"npc":"Loremaster Borannin","text":"Soandso! Thank Brell you're here. I was about to send one of my Lorekeepers looking for you. It appears that the information Tanik acquired is most perilous indeed. The Dain has called an emergency session of the council and I must attend. We don't have the luxury of waiting for an appropriate task to arise, you must advance as soon as possible. Unfortunately, I have neither the time, nor the components to fashion the next few shawls for you. Ask Rexx Frostweaver about the prayer shawl and follow his direction carefully."},{"npc":"Rexx Frostweaver","text":"Hmmm, ye be one o them offlanders, don't ye? I've heard some strange tales o yer kind so don't be tryin' any funny business with me. I know the value of a platinum piece and I'll not get cheated by yer foreign coin."},{"npc":"Rexx Frostweaver","text":"Gather five strands of crystalline silk thread and combine them in a sewing kit to make a crystalline silk fiber. Take this container and combine a glowing shardworm bile with three of the fibers to form a piece of glowing crystalline silk. Five pieces of glowing crystalline silk sewn to your fur-lined shawl will yield a beautiful silk shawl. Become a master in the art of tailoring before risking all you've worked for and be sure to let me inspect your work when it's complete."},{"npc":"Rexx Frostweaver","text":"Splendid, Soandso, this is beautiful workmanship! As the Grand Historian may have mentioned, our esteemed Dain Frostreaver the fourth is making some important plans with his council. These plans will doubtlessly include you if the Dain deems you worthy."},{"npc":"Rexx Frostweaver","text":"To ensure your worthiness you must continue to refine your prayer shawl. Speak with my wife Betti regarding the embroidered shawl and listen carefully to her words. Hurry now, there seems to be a sense of urgency about."},{"npc":"Betti Frostweaver","text":"Well, hello there, dear, it sure gets cold here, doesn't it? Perhaps I can interest you in a sewing pattern to pass the time and keep you warm."},{"npc":"Betti Frostweaver","text":"It will be an honor to assist you in fashioning an embroidered shawl. It is a very demanding product and I can see from the look in your eyes that you desire to burn your sewing kit in our furnace (YEP), but if you persevere, your efforts will be richly rewarded. When you are ready you must carefully weave a spool of sacred Coldain thread. Take the thread, this pattern, and the silk shawl and carefully embroider the pattern. The result will be most exquisite. Please show me if you manage to create one."},{"npc":"Betti Frostweaver","text":"Take a woven frost giant beard, two siren's hairs, two manticore manes and two Drakkel dire wolf whiskers, and combine them in a sewing kit. The resulting thread will enhance your shawl's power when embroidered in a special pattern."},{"npc":"Betti Frostweaver","text":"Spectacular artistry! I doubt I could have done better myself. You'll have to forgive me, I know time is short and I tend to carry on. This is the pattern for the making of a rune sacred to our people. It will be our final test of your craftsmanship and will put many of your skills to the test, but I trust you'll find the finished product to be more than worth the effort. Show Gilthan the silk shawl, he will set you on the path. May Brell always be with you outlander."},{"npc":"Gilthan Brittleblade","text":"So, you've been chosen to attempt the rune, eh? Been ages since anyone's even made an attempt. The rune represents the very essence of our people, our culture, and our religion. Take a sea shell runed with enduring breath and a small brick of velium and grind them together in a mortar and pestle. Add water to the powder and model the rune. Fire the rune with water and the best of firing sheets. Show the product to Trademaster Kroven."},{"npc":"Trademaster Kroven","text":"Fine piece of work there, Soandso, especially fer an outlander. Now yer gunna need to make a burin to etch the rune with. Once that's done ye need to kneel in the chapel and recite this prayer with total sincerity in yer heart. If yer plea be heard by our Father Brell he'll bless ya with the knowledge necessary to carry on. With that knowledge you'll take the blank rune, the burin and a fletching kit to etch the rune. Show Grimthor the etched rune and he'll guide you from there."},{"npc":"Trademaster Kroven","text":"You'll need a fletching kit and a fair bit of skill for this one, Soandso. Round up a tooth from a swordfish and attatch it to an Ulthork tusk wrapped in a Molkor hide."},{"npc":"Grimthor Brewbeard","text":"Grab a pole and fish the waters in Iceclad until you catch yourself three Iceclad Cutlass fish. Place them in this oil extractor and you'll have whatcha need."},{"npc":"Grimthor Brewbeard","text":"Collect a small piece of velium and a bottle of rubbing alcohol and brew them together in a barrel. It aint easy, but it should prove to be a minor task for the likes of you."},{"npc":"Talem Tucter","text":"I've heard of your mission, Soandso. I must admit that I had my doubts you'd make it this far. The rune's creation is nearly impossible for even the most skilled of Coldain craftsmen. You should be exceedingly proud. Many have attempted this feat and nearly all have lacked the skill, faith, patience and persistence that is prerequisite for what destiny holds in store for you. You are now ready to use this pattern to construct the sacred rune's casing and complete the runed shawl."},{"npc":"Talem Tucter","text":"Combine two platinum bars, a small piece of velium and the casing pattern in a Jeweler's kit. Take the completed casing and the rune and combine them in the same kit. When this is done all that's left is to tailor the rune to the shawl with the pattern. Take the finished product to Borannin, I'm sure he's eager to speak with you."},{"npc":"Loremaster Borannin","text":"Incredible! Never before has an outlander been skilled and determined enough to craft our sacred rune. You are now worthy of the Dains most perilous tasks. One is being prepared for you as we speak, please check back with me soon and I will outline the details for you. Until then, Fastsole, allow me to commend you on a job well done!"},{"npc":"Guard Leif","text":"Well I'll be derned. An outlander that can make a good Bearmeat 'n Bread! Thank ye, Soandso."}],"fetchedAt":"2026-09-16T09:33:08.139Z","outOfEra":true}
Going Postal	25	{"kind":"quest","title":"Going Postal","wikiPath":"/Going_Postal","sources":[{"kind":"quest","where":"Various","detail":"Start zone"},{"kind":"quest","where":"Various","detail":"Quest giver"}],"components":[],"rewards":[{"text":"Faction","item":"Faction","wikiPath":"/Faction"},{"text":"Experience"},{"text":"Small Coin"}],"card":{"title":"Going Postal","lines":["Minimum Level: 1+","Classes: All","Related Zones: Various","Related NPCs: Various"]},"links":["Faction","League of Antonican Bards","Knights of Truth","Guards of Qeynos","Ring of Scale","Mayong Mistmoore (Faction)","Ak'Anon","Kelethin","Lyra Lyrestringer","Jakum Webdancer","Butcherblock","Siltria Marwind","Erudin","Qeynos","Ticar Lorestring","Tralyn Marsinger","Feerrott","Freeport","Drizda Tunesinger","Felisity Starbright","Felwithe","Tacar Tissleplay","Ton Twostring","Idia","High Keep","Lislia Goldtune","Eve Marsinger","Halas","Marton Stringsinger","Innothule Swamp","Dark Deathsinger","Kaladim","Kilam Oresinger","Nektulos","Travis Two Tone","Rivervale","Silna Songsmith","Surefall Glade","Sivina Lutewhisper","West Karana","Mistrana Two Notes","Bard Mail"],"dialogue":[{"npc":"Lyra Lyrestringer","text":"Hail, ______ - Are you [interested] in helping the League of Antonican Bards by delivering some [mail]?"},{"npc":"Lyra Lyrestringer","text":"The League of Antonican Bards has a courier system made up of travelers and adventurers. We pay good gold to anyone who will take messages from bards such as myself to one of our more central offices. Are you [interested]?"},{"npc":"Lyra Lyrestringer","text":"I have messages that need to go to - well, right now I have one that needs to go to Kelethin. Will you [deliver] mail to [Kelethin] for me?"},{"npc":"Lyra Lyrestringer","text":"Take this letter to Jakum Webdancer in Kelethin. You can find him at the bard guild hall. I am sure he will compensate you for your troubles."}],"fetchedAt":"2026-09-16T09:43:38.263Z","outOfEra":false}
The Bread Shipment (Neriak)	25	{"kind":"quest","title":"The Bread Shipment (Neriak)","wikiPath":"/The_Bread_Shipment_(Neriak)","sources":[{"kind":"quest","where":"Neriak Foreign Quarter","detail":"Start zone"},{"kind":"quest","where":"Sal Drana","detail":"Quest giver"}],"components":[{"name":"Bag of Bread Loaves","qty":1,"wikiPath":"/Bag_of_Bread_Loaves"}],"rewards":[{"text":"Faction, Experience, Coin"}],"card":{"title":"The Bread Shipment (Neriak)","lines":["Minimum Level: 1","Classes: All","Related Zones: Southern Karana","Related NPCs: Jarlen Meadowgreen"]},"links":["Neriak","Sal Drana","Southern Karana","Jarlen Meadowgreen","Faction","Muffin Quests","Bag of Bread Loaves","Runnyeye","Dark Bargainers","Dreadguard Outer","Dreadguard Inner"],"dialogue":[{"npc":"Sal Drana","text":"Greetings to you. It seems we have a bit of a food shortage. I'm afraid I may be out of certain supplies. However, King Thex in his benevolent wisdom has authorized us merchants to look to the Teir`Dal and those friendly to our causes for assistance with this matter. Would you be [willing to assist] us?"},{"npc":"Sal Drana","text":"Very well. There are two ways you may help us to keep our supplies stocked. If you are a [baker] you may use your skills to personally keep our supplies maintained at acceptable levels. If you are willing to travel then you can help us keep the supply lines open by personally delivering [food shipments]. You will be compensated in either case."},{"npc":"Sal Drana","text":"An adventurous sort, very good. Then travel to the Southern Plains of Karana and locate the centaur baker there. He has a large supply of grain and we have been authorized to secure shipments of bread loaves from this individual. Tell him you are there to secure of shipment of bread loaves for the people of Neriak. You shall be compensated upon your return."},{"npc":"Sal Drana","text":"You have returned and none too soon! Thank you very much, I will put this bread on sale immediately. Here is your reward as promised. Thank you very much."},{"npc":"Jarlen Meadowgreen","text":"So, ya want some of my bread is that it? Well, you've come to the right place I'd say. My brothers told me the market was ripe for that sort of thing so I decided to move on over here. Anyway, hand over two gold pieces and I'll give ya a sack of bread made by me own two hands."}],"fetchedAt":"2026-09-16T09:54:21.178Z","outOfEra":false}
